1
00:00:03,380 --> 00:00:04,923
Oops. A little help.

2
00:00:07,884 --> 00:00:10,011
Wow, your hair is really thinning.

3
00:00:10,804 --> 00:00:14,015
Standing is proven to be healthier, increases productivity

4
00:00:14,099 --> 00:00:15,392
and just looks cooler.

5
00:00:16,101 --> 00:00:18,269
Picture someone doing something heroic.

6
00:00:18,353 --> 00:00:20,605
Now, was he sitting or standing?

7
00:00:21,564 --> 00:00:22,774
Not counting FDR.

8
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:25,527
Every second you sit there is an hour off your life.

9
00:00:25,610 --> 00:00:27,445
Look at all of you.

10
00:00:27,946 --> 00:00:29,572
I feel like you're in a suicide cult.

11
00:00:29,698 --> 00:00:32,367
No,no,no. You're way off on that one.

12
00:00:32,450 --> 00:00:34,494
Are you really comfortable standing there?

13
00:00:34,577 --> 00:00:37,706
I tried one of those, and I just couldn't find the sweet spot.

14
00:00:41,668 --> 00:00:44,671
Hey, guys, let's just all admit it, okay? Dwight's better than us.

15
00:00:45,046 --> 00:00:47,090
He had the guts to stop sitting,

16
00:00:47,173 --> 00:00:49,884
and he's never, ever gonna go back on it, right?

17
00:00:50,301 --> 00:00:51,428
That's right, Jim.

18
00:01:01,646 --> 00:01:02,814
Hey, man. Hey.

19
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:04,941
Taking a load off, huh?

20
00:01:05,066 --> 00:01:06,609
No. Putting a load on, more like.

21
00:01:06,901 --> 00:01:07,986
Good luck with that.

22
00:01:08,153 --> 00:01:09,446
Last thing I need is luck.

23
00:01:15,827 --> 00:01:17,036
Thank you so much.

24
00:01:34,137 --> 00:01:35,722
What are you up to? Oh, look out.

25
00:01:35,847 --> 00:01:36,890
Just... What are you doing?

26
00:01:37,015 --> 00:01:38,099
Think fast. Ha ha!

27
00:01:38,391 --> 00:01:40,185
Give that back. Come on. Prank!

28
00:01:41,352 --> 00:01:42,604
That's real creative.

29
00:01:42,687 --> 00:01:43,855
You know what, you're right. It's not my best.

30
00:01:44,022 --> 00:01:45,148
'Cause you could easily just bend over

31
00:01:45,231 --> 00:01:46,274
and pick that up, right?

32
00:01:46,357 --> 00:01:48,234
I could. I just don't feel like it, loser.

33
00:01:48,318 --> 00:01:49,444
Because you're sitting? Standing.

34
00:01:49,527 --> 00:01:51,029
Okay. Don't!

35
00:01:51,362 --> 00:01:52,697
Because you're sitting? Standing.

36
00:01:53,281 --> 00:01:54,365
You know I have to do this.

37
00:01:55,533 --> 00:01:56,493
I know.

38
00:01:56,576 --> 00:01:57,577
Whoa!

39
00:02:19,933 --> 00:02:23,895
Andrew Baines Bernard.

40
00:02:24,020 --> 00:02:25,814
I think you could just do Andy Bernard.

41
00:02:25,897 --> 00:02:28,316
Andrew Baines Bernard. I love filling

42
00:02:28,441 --> 00:02:30,902
these out 'cause it's like, Oh, I'm taking a test,

43
00:02:30,985 --> 00:02:32,529
but I know the answers.

44
00:02:33,404 --> 00:02:37,283
In four seconds, my wife is going to be coming through that door.

45
00:02:37,408 --> 00:02:38,493
I told her she could work here.

46
00:02:38,576 --> 00:02:41,329
Under no circumstances can that be allowed to happen.

47
00:02:43,373 --> 00:02:44,958
There you are, honey.

48
00:02:45,083 --> 00:02:47,126
How on earth did you miss the elevator?

49
00:02:47,210 --> 00:02:48,169
What was that?

50
00:02:48,253 --> 00:02:49,671
I don't know. He wasn't talking to me.

51
00:02:49,754 --> 00:02:52,257
But if I were you, I wouldn't hire his wife.

52
00:02:53,591 --> 00:02:55,176
That's why my foundation,

53
00:02:55,260 --> 00:02:56,386
the Dream For A Wish Foundation,

54
00:02:56,469 --> 00:02:57,637
is gonna put them out of business.

55
00:02:57,762 --> 00:03:00,056
They're not gonna know what hit them.

56
00:03:00,139 --> 00:03:03,268
Everyone, I'd like to introduce my wife,

57
00:03:03,351 --> 00:03:04,853
Mrs. Robert California.

58
00:03:04,936 --> 00:03:07,146
Mrs. California, this is everyone.

59
00:03:07,272 --> 00:03:08,273
Hello. Hi.

60
00:03:08,356 --> 00:03:10,358
Welcome. Call me Susan, please.

61
00:03:10,441 --> 00:03:13,862
Last night at dinner, Susan and I were talking

62
00:03:13,945 --> 00:03:15,488
about her returning to work.

63
00:03:15,864 --> 00:03:19,200
So she's here today to see if there's a good fit.

64
00:03:19,284 --> 00:03:21,661
Something tells me it just might work out.

65
00:03:22,954 --> 00:03:25,874
This is Andy Bernard, the regional manager.

66
00:03:25,957 --> 00:03:27,041
Hello. Nice to meet you.

67
00:03:27,166 --> 00:03:28,209
Hey there. It's a pleasure. Welcome.

68
00:03:28,293 --> 00:03:29,294
Thank you.

69
00:03:29,377 --> 00:03:30,920
Andy, would you be so kind

70
00:03:31,004 --> 00:03:32,714
as to show Susan around the office,

71
00:03:32,797 --> 00:03:34,799
introduce her to various departments,

72
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:37,135
find a place where she'll shine?

73
00:03:37,343 --> 00:03:40,054
I would love to, but I have to be

74
00:03:40,138 --> 00:03:41,598
completely honest with you guys.

75
00:03:42,265 --> 00:03:43,558
We're 100% staffed up.

76
00:03:46,227 --> 00:03:49,814
Andy, let's see if there's a good fit first, then we'll talk.

77
00:03:53,943 --> 00:03:55,278
All right.

78
00:03:55,695 --> 00:03:57,572
Knock, knock, knock Knock, knock, knock

79
00:03:57,697 --> 00:03:59,449
You don't have to say it if you're doing it.

80
00:03:59,532 --> 00:04:01,576
Remember how you said

81
00:04:01,659 --> 00:04:03,912
that you were looking for a place in the office

82
00:04:03,995 --> 00:04:06,331
to do calisthenics and aerobics?

83
00:04:07,498 --> 00:04:09,000
Ah, weightlifting, yeah.

84
00:04:09,375 --> 00:04:10,418
Well, today's your lucky day.

85
00:04:10,501 --> 00:04:12,712
I have opened, in this very office building,

86
00:04:12,837 --> 00:04:15,089
Dwight Schrute's Gym for Muscles.

87
00:04:15,340 --> 00:04:17,175
Want to take a look? I'll take a look.

88
00:04:17,508 --> 00:04:21,179
Your path from obesity begins right here.

89
00:04:23,014 --> 00:04:26,100
I've been meaning to join a gym. For my health.

90
00:04:26,517 --> 00:04:29,520
<i>I used to say I wanted to live long enough to see</i> a <i>black president</i>

91
00:04:29,646 --> 00:04:31,356
I didn't realize how easy that would be.

92
00:04:31,522 --> 00:04:32,732
<i>So now I want to live long enough</i>

93
00:04:32,815 --> 00:04:35,318
to see a really, really gay president

94
00:04:35,485 --> 00:04:36,694
or a supermodel president.

95
00:04:37,278 --> 00:04:39,572
I want to see all the different kinds of presidents.

96
00:04:40,114 --> 00:04:42,867
Obese people in my office building are a drain on resources.

97
00:04:43,159 --> 00:04:44,577
Chairs wear out faster.

98
00:04:44,786 --> 00:04:46,537
It takes more freon to keep them cool.

99
00:04:46,621 --> 00:04:48,206
They flush the toilets more often.

100
00:04:48,289 --> 00:04:51,167
Plus, their massive BMs bust the rivets on my pipes.

101
00:04:52,043 --> 00:04:56,214
But a gym turns fat into cash.

102
00:04:57,256 --> 00:05:00,176
All right, the DM Express is pulling out.

103
00:05:00,259 --> 00:05:01,886
All right, well, it was really nice to meet you, Brian.

104
00:05:02,011 --> 00:05:03,137
Ah, it's actually Ryan.

105
00:05:03,221 --> 00:05:04,555
Oh, Ryan. Yeah.

106
00:05:05,390 --> 00:05:06,557
Bitch.

107
00:05:07,225 --> 00:05:09,602
We will start here at Erinville.

108
00:05:09,686 --> 00:05:10,687
Hi.

109
00:05:10,812 --> 00:05:12,230
Reception.

110
00:05:12,313 --> 00:05:13,940
Your classic one-man operation.

111
00:05:14,065 --> 00:05:15,650
Although, I was watching a movie,

112
00:05:15,775 --> 00:05:17,402
and Meryl Streep had two secretaries.

113
00:05:17,485 --> 00:05:20,446
I was watching a movie, and a bunch of apes took over San Francisco.

114
00:05:20,822 --> 00:05:21,823
Just saying.

115
00:05:21,906 --> 00:05:25,410
Two secretaries could convey a sense of importance

116
00:05:25,576 --> 00:05:27,120
and success to our clients.

117
00:05:27,286 --> 00:05:30,623
Certainly worth exploring. Wouldn't you agree, Andy?

118
00:05:31,582 --> 00:05:33,584
- I'll explore exploring it. - Good.

119
00:05:33,835 --> 00:05:35,837
Seems like you have this under control,

120
00:05:35,962 --> 00:05:38,506
so I'll just duck out and run the company for a while.

121
00:05:38,589 --> 00:05:39,590
Okay.

122
00:05:43,636 --> 00:05:46,514
Okay, next stop on the tour, sales.

123
00:05:46,848 --> 00:05:49,851
Here we go. Station stop, Jim Halpert.

124
00:05:49,934 --> 00:05:51,936
Oh, boy, our resident truth teller. Uh...

125
00:05:52,103 --> 00:05:53,563
All right, have at it. Let her rip.

126
00:05:53,688 --> 00:05:55,106
What do you hate about this place?

127
00:05:56,691 --> 00:05:58,651
Well, it's sales, so you have to be able

128
00:05:58,776 --> 00:06:00,778
to live in the world of rejection.

129
00:06:00,903 --> 00:06:02,363
Maybe you do.

130
00:06:02,613 --> 00:06:03,948
Hi, I'm Dwight.

131
00:06:04,115 --> 00:06:07,744
Sales is really not so hard, okay. It's paper.

132
00:06:08,077 --> 00:06:09,537
We have it, and they want it so bad

133
00:06:09,662 --> 00:06:11,122
they are willing to pay for it.

134
00:06:11,289 --> 00:06:12,290
Jim?

135
00:06:12,373 --> 00:06:14,625
Well, it's not that easy.

136
00:06:14,709 --> 00:06:16,210
It's kind of sometimes difficult.

137
00:06:16,627 --> 00:06:18,713
It's the second-easiest job in the world.

138
00:06:18,921 --> 00:06:20,673
Being a mom. I love shopping.

139
00:06:21,174 --> 00:06:23,134
And sales is just the other side of that.

140
00:06:23,301 --> 00:06:25,094
That's true.

141
00:06:25,803 --> 00:06:29,140
You know, if you joined our sales department,

142
00:06:29,223 --> 00:06:31,100
you would be working very closely with our

143
00:06:31,225 --> 00:06:33,102
department head, Mr. Dwight Schrute.

144
00:06:33,186 --> 00:06:34,187
That's me.

145
00:06:34,353 --> 00:06:37,231
Dwight, why don't you tell Susan about some of your hobbies.

146
00:06:37,648 --> 00:06:39,400
Oh... Mmm-hmm. Survival skills.

147
00:06:39,817 --> 00:06:41,235
Ranking of animals.

148
00:06:41,444 --> 00:06:42,779
Maybe over a beer

149
00:06:42,862 --> 00:06:45,823
after she's closed her first sale.

150
00:06:47,033 --> 00:06:50,536
Well, make that a red wine and I'll tell you my animal rankings.

151
00:06:53,331 --> 00:06:56,125
How am I supposed to pull this off?

152
00:06:56,501 --> 00:06:59,754
The entire office is being nicer to her than they've ever been to me.

153
00:06:59,837 --> 00:07:01,464
What I wouldn't give for one of Phyllis'

154
00:07:01,547 --> 00:07:03,341
classic room-clearing farts right now.

155
00:07:04,675 --> 00:07:05,843
Ready?

156
00:07:09,555 --> 00:07:11,140
What do you think? Huh?

157
00:07:11,224 --> 00:07:12,850
Umm, no.

158
00:07:12,934 --> 00:07:14,102
No. This is not a gym.

159
00:07:14,185 --> 00:07:15,812
This is like a scene out of Saw V.

160
00:07:15,895 --> 00:07:17,355
You haven't even looked around yet.

161
00:07:17,438 --> 00:07:18,606
Look.

162
00:07:18,856 --> 00:07:20,983
Gravel bucket squat yoke.

163
00:07:24,654 --> 00:07:26,197
Right?

164
00:07:26,447 --> 00:07:27,448
Hmm.

165
00:07:28,074 --> 00:07:29,867
Dedicated phone book ripping station.

166
00:07:32,495 --> 00:07:34,288
You ever cut tin before? No.

167
00:07:34,664 --> 00:07:37,542
Five yards in and your forearms will be on fire.

168
00:07:37,750 --> 00:07:39,293
Plus, I will buy the tin back from you

169
00:07:39,418 --> 00:07:41,003
that you cut for two cents a yard.

170
00:07:42,296 --> 00:07:44,132
Now, let's go over membership.

171
00:07:44,215 --> 00:07:45,883
I'm gonna need the first month's

172
00:07:45,967 --> 00:07:48,302
and the last month's up front for $49 a month.

173
00:07:48,761 --> 00:07:51,347
But every third month is $59 a month.

174
00:07:51,472 --> 00:07:55,059
But the fourth month is a discount month at $19 per month.

175
00:07:55,184 --> 00:07:57,645
Obviously, you know how a gym works.

176
00:07:58,229 --> 00:08:00,189
So you know I'm not gonna pay money for this.

177
00:08:00,398 --> 00:08:01,941
You want people to come to your gym?

178
00:08:02,233 --> 00:08:03,901
Make a real gym.

179
00:08:04,318 --> 00:08:05,570
Darryl.

180
00:08:08,531 --> 00:08:09,699
Make a real gym.

181
00:08:09,907 --> 00:08:12,577
I was thinking accounting might be a good fit

182
00:08:12,660 --> 00:08:14,036
because I really clicked with Oscar,

183
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:16,706
and I do have some experience with bookkeeping.

184
00:08:16,914 --> 00:08:20,251
But we already have a surplus of accountants as it is.

185
00:08:20,418 --> 00:08:23,921
I would work in customer service, um, HR, even.

186
00:08:24,005 --> 00:08:25,840
Those are fully staffed as well.

187
00:08:25,923 --> 00:08:29,510
Are you telling me that there's no one in this entire office

188
00:08:29,594 --> 00:08:32,096
that could use an extra pair of hands?

189
00:08:32,930 --> 00:08:34,015
Yes.

190
00:08:34,098 --> 00:08:39,270
I am the CEO, and I am telling an employee of mine what to do.

191
00:08:40,438 --> 00:08:42,648
Let me beat around the bush for a second.

192
00:08:43,107 --> 00:08:46,861
Our chairman of the board has some very strong feelings...

193
00:08:46,944 --> 00:08:49,697
Robert, it's all right. This is very uncomfortable.

194
00:08:49,780 --> 00:08:53,826
Obviously, there's no place for me here, so thank you for trying.

195
00:08:53,910 --> 00:08:54,911
Why don't we just let it go?

196
00:08:55,036 --> 00:08:56,037
No. Absolutely not.

197
00:08:56,120 --> 00:08:58,581
Andrew, there must be something you can do.

198
00:08:58,664 --> 00:08:59,999
There must be. Think.

199
00:09:02,251 --> 00:09:03,920
Well, there are a lot of considerations.

200
00:09:04,003 --> 00:09:07,632
I would be eternally grateful.

201
00:09:09,133 --> 00:09:12,637
It's not a bad thing to have the CEO owe you one.

202
00:09:16,474 --> 00:09:19,310
All right! Well, then, welcome aboard.

203
00:09:27,693 --> 00:09:28,819
So what happens next?

204
00:09:28,945 --> 00:09:33,449
We get you over to HR and then get you set up with accounting.

205
00:09:34,659 --> 00:09:35,785
Hang on.

206
00:09:35,910 --> 00:09:37,870
- Hello? - Say "hello, grandma."

207
00:09:39,956 --> 00:09:41,332
Hi, gam-gam.

208
00:09:41,499 --> 00:09:44,043
Hold one finger up to Susan. You'll just be a second.

209
00:09:45,461 --> 00:09:46,879
You numbskull!

210
00:09:46,963 --> 00:09:48,506
You were given a very simple task.

211
00:09:48,589 --> 00:09:50,591
I could not have been more clear with you.

212
00:09:51,300 --> 00:09:52,927
Now say, "Are you taking your medicine?"

213
00:09:53,386 --> 00:09:55,221
Are you taking your med-meds?

214
00:09:55,346 --> 00:09:58,224
Why can you not say exactly what I tell you?

215
00:09:58,349 --> 00:10:01,435
Undo this. Undo it.

216
00:10:05,564 --> 00:10:07,191
You didn't say good-bye to your grandmother.

217
00:10:07,942 --> 00:10:09,819
We promised we'd never say good-bye.

218
00:10:14,282 --> 00:10:17,159
Attention! I am now accepting memberships

219
00:10:17,243 --> 00:10:19,453
for the Dwight Schrute Gym for Muscles.

220
00:10:19,870 --> 00:10:21,622
First 20 members can take advantage

221
00:10:21,706 --> 00:10:23,791
of our "pay what you weigh" promotion.

222
00:10:23,874 --> 00:10:25,418
All I need is another gym.

223
00:10:25,584 --> 00:10:26,752
As if I don't have enough drama.

224
00:10:26,877 --> 00:10:29,672
We have a gym at home. It's called the bedroom.

225
00:10:29,755 --> 00:10:30,881
Who's spotting who?

226
00:10:31,048 --> 00:10:32,383
"Don't use the bike in the corner,

227
00:10:32,550 --> 00:10:33,926
"that's Bruce's. Jeremy says..."

228
00:10:34,010 --> 00:10:35,344
Enough. Oscar, enough.

229
00:10:35,428 --> 00:10:36,929
Kelly? I have these sneakers,

230
00:10:37,096 --> 00:10:39,473
which are basically just like a gym for your feet, so...

231
00:10:42,476 --> 00:10:44,770
That's okay. I know how to build a business.

232
00:10:45,146 --> 00:10:46,564
You gotta bet the black people to do it

233
00:10:46,731 --> 00:10:48,190
to get the white people to do it.

234
00:10:48,607 --> 00:10:50,735
Then you gotta get the black people to stop doing it.

235
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:52,737
One step at a time.

236
00:10:53,237 --> 00:10:54,905
Did you bring your passport with you?

237
00:10:55,448 --> 00:10:56,741
Who walks around with their passport?

238
00:10:56,824 --> 00:10:57,825
Well, I do.

239
00:10:57,908 --> 00:10:58,993
Always ready for adventure.

240
00:10:59,076 --> 00:11:00,453
Have you had any?

241
00:11:00,661 --> 00:11:01,704
No.

242
00:11:06,417 --> 00:11:07,752
Hey, GUYS

243
00:11:08,377 --> 00:11:11,255
So Robert doesn't want his wife working here.

244
00:11:11,422 --> 00:11:13,841
So now that she is, we have to drive her away.

245
00:11:14,258 --> 00:11:18,054
Andy, if he didn't want her working here, then why did you hire her?

246
00:11:18,304 --> 00:11:21,349
Oscar, it was a mistake.

247
00:11:21,974 --> 00:11:25,269
But one that can be fixed by all of us being mean to her.

248
00:11:25,519 --> 00:11:28,773
How can we do that? She's simply wonderful.

249
00:11:28,981 --> 00:11:30,149
This is all pathetic.

250
00:11:30,316 --> 00:11:32,943
I am not asking, lam ordering.

251
00:11:33,778 --> 00:11:35,196
How mean are we talking about?

252
00:11:35,321 --> 00:11:36,447
It would be great if she were gone by lunch.

253
00:11:37,281 --> 00:11:39,909
Erin, you're up. Find her a place to work, but not too comfortable.

254
00:11:39,992 --> 00:11:42,411
Got it. I know exactly which stapler to give her.

255
00:11:46,749 --> 00:11:48,292
Here you go.

256
00:11:51,962 --> 00:11:53,381
Um, do you think it would be possible

257
00:11:53,506 --> 00:11:54,965
to move to that desk over there?

258
00:11:55,049 --> 00:11:58,219
Because this seems a bit cramped, and I don't have a computer.

259
00:11:58,386 --> 00:11:59,720
Well, that's a sales desk.

260
00:11:59,804 --> 00:12:02,598
Yeah. You need to be over here with us accountants.

261
00:12:03,015 --> 00:12:05,142
Just sit here and be quiet.

262
00:12:05,559 --> 00:12:08,312
And if you have a question, just raise your hand.

